stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(individual will of the subject adopts without reflection the conduct and) Tj T*
(habit prescribed by justice and the laws. The individual is, therefore,) Tj T*
(in unconscious unity with the idea--the social weal.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The third phase is the realm of abstract universality \(in which the) Tj T*
(social aim absorbs all individual aims\); it is the Roman state, the) Tj T*
(severe labours of the manhood of history. For true manhood acts neither) Tj T*
(in accordance with the caprice of a despot nor in obedience to a) Tj T*
(graceful caprice of its own. It works for a general aim, one in which) Tj T*
(the individual perishes and realises his own private object only in that) Tj T*
(general aim. The state begins to have an abstract existence and to) Tj T*
(develop itself for a definite object, in accomplishing which its members) Tj T*
(have indeed a share, but not a complete and concrete one \(calling their) Tj T*
(whole being into play\). Free individuals are sacrificed to the severe) Tj T*
(demands of the national ends, to which they must surrender themselves in) Tj T*
(this service of abstract generalisation. The Roman state is not a) Tj T*
(repetition of such a state of individuals as was the Athenian _polis_.) Tj T*
(The geniality and joy of soul that existed there have given place to) Tj T*
(harsh and rigorous toil. The interest of history is detached from) Tj T*
(individuals.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(But when, subsequently, in the historical development, individuality) Tj T*
(gains the ascendant, and the breaking up of the community into its) Tj T*
(component atoms can be restrained only by external compulsion, then the) Tj T*
(subjective might of individual despotism comes forward to play its part.) Tj T*
(The individual is led to seek consolation for the loss of his freedom in) Tj T*
(exercising and developing his private rights. In the next place, the) Tj T*
(pain inflicted by despotism begins to be felt, and spirit, driven back) Tj T*
(into its utmost depths, leaves the godless world, seeks for a harmony in) Tj T*
(itself, and begins now an inner life--a complete concrete subjectivity,) Tj T*
(which at the same time possesses a substantiality that is not grounded) Tj T*
(in mere external existence.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Within the soul, therefore, arises the spiritual solution of the) Tj T*
(struggle, in the fact that the individual personality, instead of) Tj T*
(following its own capricious choice, is purified and elevated into) Tj T*
(universality--a subjectivity that of its own free will adopts principles) Tj T*
(tending to the good of all, reaches, in fact, a divine personality. To) Tj T*
(the worldly empire this spiritual one wears a predominant aspect of) Tj T*
(opposition, as the empire of subjectivity that has attained to the) Tj T*
(knowledge of itself--itself in its essential nature--the empire of) Tj T*
(spirit in its full sense.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Christian community found itself in the Roman world, but as it was) Tj T*
(secluded from this state, and did not hold the emperor for its absolute) Tj T*
(sovereign, it was the object of persecution. Then was manifested its) Tj T*
(inward liberty in the steadfastness with which sufferings were borne. As) Tj T*
(regards its relation to the truth, the fathers of the Church built up) Tj T*
(the dogma, but a chief element was furnished by the previous development) Tj T*
(of philosophy. Just as Philo found a deeper import shadowed forth in the) Tj T*
(Mosaic record and idealised what he considered the bare shell of the) Tj T*
(narrative, so also did the Christians treat their records.) Tj T*
ET
