(unity of all conditions of thought. So all transcendental ideas may be) Tj T*
(arranged in three classes; the first containing the unity of the) Tj T*
(thinking subject; the second, the unity of the conditions of phenomena) Tj T*
(observed; the third, the unity of the objective conditions of thought.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This classification becomes clear if we note that the thinking subject) Tj T*
(is the object-matter of psychology; while the system of all phenomena) Tj T*
(\(the world\) is the object-matter of cosmology; and the Being of all) Tj T*
(Beings \(God\) is the object-matter of theology.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Hence we perceive that pure reason supplies three transcendental ideas,) Tj T*
(namely, the idea of a transcendental science of the soul \(_psychologia) Tj T*
(rationalis_\); of a transcendental science of the world \(_cosmologia) Tj T*
(rationalis_\); and, lastly, of a transcendental science of God) Tj T*
(\(_theologia transcendentalis_\). It is the glory of transcendental) Tj T*
(idealism that by it the mind ascends in the series of conditions till) Tj T*
(it reaches the unconditioned, that is, the principles. We thus progress) Tj T*
(from our knowledge of self to a knowledge of the world, and through it) Tj T*
(to a knowledge of the Supreme Being.) Tj T*
