(     critic, and it is by his splendid critical work, the "Biographical) Tj T*
(     History of Philosophy," that he is now best remembered. In this) Tj T*
(     remarkable book, which appeared in 1845-46, Lewes the novelist and) Tj T*
(     the journalist collaborates with Lewes the philosopher and man of) Tj T*
(     science. He has the rare art of making an abstruse subject clear) Tj T*
(     and attractive; he does not give a dry summary of the ideas of the) Tj T*
(     great thinkers, but depicts the living man and relates his way of) Tj T*
(     life to his way of thinking. The result is that in his hands) Tj T*
