(_I.--The Early Thinkers_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is the object of the present work to show how philosophy became a) Tj T*
(positive science; to indicate by what methods the human mind was enabled) Tj T*
(to conquer its present modicum of certain knowledge. The boldest and the) Tj T*
(grandest speculations came first. Man needed the stimulus of some higher) Tj T*
(reward than that of merely tracing the laws of phenomena. Nothing but a) Tj T*
(solution of the mystery of the universe could content him. Astronomy was) Tj T*
(derived from astrology: chemistry from alchemy, and physiology from) Tj T*
(auguries. The position occupied by philosophy in the history of mankind) Tj T*
(is that of the great initiative to positive science. It was the forlorn) Tj T*
(hope of mankind, and though it perished in its efforts, it did not) Tj T*
(perish without having led the way to victory.) Tj T*
