() Tj T*
(_II.--In My Library_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Intercourse with books comforts me in age and solaces me in) Tj T*
(solitariness, eases me of weariness and rids me of tedious company. To) Tj T*
(divert importunate thoughts there is no better way than recourse to) Tj T*
(books. And though they perceive I on occasion forsake them, they never) Tj T*
(mutiny or murmur, but welcome me always with the self-same visage.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I never travel, whether in peace or in war, without books. It is) Tj T*
(wonderful what repose I find in the knowledge that they are at my elbow) Tj T*
(to delight me when time shall serve. In this human peregrination this is) Tj T*
(the best munition I have found.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At home I betake me somewhat oftener to my library. It is in the chief) Tj T*
(approach to my house, so that under my eyes are my garden, my) Tj T*
(base-court, my yard, and even the best rooms of my house. There, without) Tj T*
(order or method, I can turn over and ransack now one book and now) Tj T*
(another. Sometimes I muse, sometimes save; and walking up and down I) Tj T*
(indite and register these my humours, these my conceits. It is placed in) Tj T*
(a third storey of a tower. The lowermost is my chapel, the second a) Tj T*
(chamber, where I often lie when I would be alone. Above is a) Tj T*
(clothes-room. In this library, formerly the least useful room in all my) Tj T*
(house, I pass the greatest part of my life's days, and most hours of the) Tj T*
(day--I am never there of nights. Next it is a handsome, neat study,) Tj T*
(large enough to have a fire in winter, and very pleasantly windowed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(If I feared not trouble more than cost I might easily join a convenient) Tj T*
(gallery of a hundred paces long and twelve broad on each side of this) Tj T*
(room, and upon the same floor, the walls being already of a convenient) Tj T*
(height. Each retired place requireth a walk. If I sit long my thoughts) Tj T*
(are prone to sleep. My mind goes not alone as if legs moved it. Those) Tj T*
(who study without books are all in the same case.) Tj T*
