(a horse for his strength and speed, not for his trappings; a greyhound) Tj T*
(for his swiftness, not his collar; a hawk for her wing, not for her) Tj T*
(bells. Why do we not likewise esteem a man for that which is his own? He) Tj T*
(has a goodly train of followers, a stately palace, so much rent coming) Tj T*
(in, so much credit among men. Alas, all that is about him, not in him.) Tj T*
