() Tj T*
(It may be suggested that I ought to be ashamed of practices which have) Tj T*
(brought you in danger of death. Risk of death is not to be taken into) Tj T*
(account in any action which really matters at all. If it ought to be,) Tj T*
(the heroes before Troy were bad characters! Every man should stand to) Tj T*
(his post, come life, come death. Should I have stood to my post and) Tj T*
(faced death when on service at Potidaca, but have failed through fear of) Tj T*
(death when the deity imposed on me a certain course of action? Whether) Tj T*
(to die be evil or good, I know not, though many think they know it to be) Tj T*
(evil. But to disobey authority, human or divine, I know to be evil; and) Tj T*
(I will not do what I know to be evil to avoid what may in fact be a) Tj T*
(good. Insomuch that if you now offer to set me free on condition that I) Tj T*
(should cease from these pursuits on pain of death, I should reply: "Men) Tj T*
(of Athens, I love and honour you, but I will obey the god rather than) Tj T*
(you; and while I breathe and have the power I will not cease from the) Tj T*
(pursuit of philosophy, or from exhorting and warning you as I have done) Tj T*
(hitherto, against caring much for riches and nothing for the perfecting) Tj T*
(of your souls. This is the bidding of the god. If to speak thus be to) Tj T*
(corrupt youth, then I corrupt youth. But he who says I speak other) Tj T*
(things than this talks vanity; and this I will do, though the penalty) Tj T*
(were many deaths.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Do not murmur, but listen, for you will profit. If you put me to death,) Tj T*
(you will harm yourselves more than me, for it is worse to do wrong than) Tj T*
(to suffer it. You will not easily find another to serve as the gadfly) Tj T*
(which rouses a noble horse--as I have done, being commissioned thereto) Tj T*
(by the god. For that I have made no profit for myself from this course,) Tj T*
(my poverty proves. If it seems absurd that I should meddle thus with) Tj T*
(each man privately, but take no part in public affairs, that is because) Tj T*
(of the divine or dæmonic influence of which I have spoken, named also in) Tj T*
(mockery by Meletus in the indictment. This is a voice which checks but) Tj T*
(never urges me on. Indeed, had I meddled with politics, I should have) Tj T*
(been dead long ago.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(That I will prove by facts. When you chose to condemn the ten generals,) Tj T*
