() Tj T*
(     The wonderful series of dialogues in which Socrates takes the) Tj T*
(     leading part are at once the foundation and the crown of all) Tj T*
(     idealistic philosophy, and as literary masterpieces remain) Tj T*
(     unmatched. Certain of Plato's disciples would claim that his) Tj T*
(     highest achievement is "The Timæus"; there are some who set their) Tj T*
(     affections on "The Phædo"; but a general vote of all Platonists) Tj T*
(     would probably give the first position to "The Republic," and this) Tj T*
(     is undoubtedly the work which has had the widest general influence.) Tj T*
