(Now for a second proof. Three kinds of pleasure correspond to the three) Tj T*
(elements of the soul--reason, spirit, desire. In each man one of the) Tj T*
(three is in the ascendant. One counts knowledge vain in comparison with) Tj T*
(the advantages of riches, another with those of honour; to the) Tj T*
(philosopher only truth counts. But he is the only one of them who makes) Tj T*
