(     The more famous son of a famous rhetorician, the Roman philosopher) Tj T*
(     L. Annæus Seneca was born at Corduba \(Cordova\), in Spain, about the) Tj T*
(     beginning of the Christian era. While the date of his birth is a) Tj T*
(     matter for conjecture, the circumstances of his death are) Tj T*
(     notorious. He was a victim of Nero's jealousy and ingratitude in 65) Tj T*
(     A.D., when the emperor seized upon a plot against himself as the) Tj T*
(     pretext for sentencing Seneca to enforced suicide. In the vivid) Tj T*
(     pages of the historian Tacitus, there are few more pathetic) Tj T*
(     descriptions than that recounting the slow ebbing of the old) Tj T*
(     philosopher's life after his veins had been opened. Seneca had) Tj T*
(     known many vicissitudes of fortune. He was banished from Rome in 41) Tj T*
(     A.D., but, after his recall, rose to great power and affluence as) Tj T*
(     tutor and adviser to Nero. His works, many of which are lost,) Tj T*
(     include tragedies, letters, and treatises on philosophy. The high) Tj T*
(     ethical standard maintained by Seneca favoured the legend that he) Tj T*
(     was influenced by the Apostle Paul, and a spurious correspondence) Tj T*
(     between them was long accepted as genuine. Of the moral works there) Tj T*
(     is, for insight into human nature and for generosity of impulse, no) Tj T*
(     better representative than that "On Benefits.") Tj T*
