(     Edward Bellamy, American social reformer, who sprang into fame in) Tj T*
(     the last decade of the nineteenth century by his book, "Looking) Tj T*
(     Backward," was born in Massachusetts, on March 25, 1850. Trained) Tj T*
(     for the Bar, he became a journalist, and devoted his pen to the) Tj T*
(     propaganda of socialism. After the unprecedented success of his) Tj T*
(     socialist novel, in which he describes a suppositious twentieth) Tj T*
(     century revolution from the standpoint of a hypnotised sleeper) Tj T*
(     awakened in 2000 A.D., his modest home at Chicopee Falls became a) Tj T*
(     recognised centre of the socialist movement in the United States.) Tj T*
(     "Looking Backward" was published in 1888, and was followed by) Tj T*
(     "Equality," in which he expounded his political doctrines in) Tj T*
