() Tj T*
(     The son of humble Polish Jews, Jean Bloch, who was born in 1836,) Tj T*
(     amassed a large fortune out of Russian railways. At the age of) Tj T*
(     fifty he retired from business, and devoted himself to an) Tj T*
(     exhaustive study of the conditions and possibilities of modern) Tj T*
(     warfare. To this labour he gave eight years, and, in 1898, the) Tj T*
(     fruits of it were published in a work of six volumes, in which he) Tj T*
(     sought to prove that, owing to the immensity of modern armies, the) Tj T*
(     deadliness of modern weapons, and the economic conditions that) Tj T*
(     prevailed in the larger states, a great European war was rapidly) Tj T*
(     becoming a physical impossibility. M. Bloch died on January 7,) Tj T*
(     1902, not before several of his theories had been tested by actual) Tj T*
(     campaigning. His main argument, however, concerns a war on European) Tj T*
(     frontiers between European powers, and such a war he did not live) Tj T*
(     to witness.) Tj T*
