(_II.--How War Will Be Waged on Land_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The bullet of the present day can kill at a vastly greater distance than) Tj T*
(the bullets fired during the Franco-German and Russo-Turkish campaigns.) Tj T*
(The powder now in use has not only far more explosive force than the) Tj T*
(old-fashioned powder, but is almost smokeless. The introduction of the) Tj T*
(magazine rifle has immensely increased the speed of firing. Moreover,) Tj T*
(the rifle is undergoing constant improvement, and becoming a more and) Tj T*
(more deadly weapon. It is easy, then, to see the following consequences) Tj T*
(from these changes: \(1\) The opening of battles from much greater) Tj T*
(distances than formerly; \(2\) the necessity of loose formation in attack;) Tj T*
(\(3\) the strengthening of the defence; \(4\) the increase in the area of) Tj T*
(the battlefield; and \(5\) the increase in casualties.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
