(AUGUSTE COMTE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A Course of Positive Philosophy) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     Isidore Auguste Marie François Xavier Comte, the founder of the) Tj T*
(     Positive philosophy, was born at Montpellier, in France, Jan. 19,) Tj T*
(     1798. Entering the Ecole Polytechnique at Paris in his seventeenth) Tj T*
(     year, he showed mathematical talent, but was expelled for) Tj T*
(     insubordination. In 1818 he met St. Simon, and for six years he) Tj T*
(     remained under the influence of that philosopher; but in 1824 he) Tj T*
(     broke away and entered on an independent philosophical career. In) Tj T*
(     1826 he expounded to a distinguished audience his system of) Tj T*
(     Positive philosophy, but during the course had an attack of) Tj T*
(     insanity which lasted for a few months. Between 1830 and 1842 he) Tj T*
(     published his "Cours de Philosophie Positive." From 1835 to 1845 he) Tj T*
(     acted as examiner at the Ecole Polytechnique, but after 1845 he was) Tj T*
(     supported by a "subsidy" from his admirers. Comte married in 1825,) Tj T*
(     but his marriage was not happy, and ended in a separation in 1842.) Tj T*
(     He died on September 5, 1857. His other important works are "The) Tj T*
(     System of Positive Politics" and the "Positivist Catechism.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_I.--Positive Classification of the Sciences_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(On studying the development of human intelligence, it is found that it) Tj T*
(passes through three stages: \(1\) The theological, \(2\) the metaphysical,) Tj T*
(\(3\) the scientific or positive. In the theological stage it seeks to) Tj T*
(account for the world by supernatural beings. In the metaphysical stage) Tj T*
(it seeks an explanation in abstract forces. In the scientific, or) Tj T*
(positive, stage it applies itself to the study of the relation of) Tj T*
(phenomena to each other.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Different sciences have passed through these stages at different rates.) Tj T*
(Astronomy reached the positive stage first, then terrestrial physics,) Tj T*
(then chemistry, then physiology, while sociology has not even yet) Tj T*
(reached it. To put social phenomena upon a positive basis is the main) Tj T*
(object of this work; its secondary object is to show that all branches) Tj T*
(of knowledge spring from the same trunk. An integration of the sciences) Tj T*
(on a positive basis should lead to the discovery of the laws which rule) Tj T*
(the intellect in the investigation of facts, should regenerate science) Tj T*
(and reorganise society. At present the theological, the metaphysical,) Tj T*
(and the positive conflict, and cause intellectual disorder and) Tj T*
(confusion.) Tj T*
ET
