() Tj T*
(The first step to be taken in forming a positive philosophy is to) Tj T*
(classify the sciences. The first great division we notice in natural) Tj T*
(phenomena is the division into inorganic and organic phenomena. Under) Tj T*
(the inorganic we may include the sciences astronomy, physics, chemistry;) Tj T*
(and under the organic we include the sciences physiology and sociology.) Tj T*
(These five sciences, astronomy, physics, chemistry, physiology, and) Tj T*
(sociology, we may consider the five fundamental sciences. This) Tj T*
(classification follows the order of the development of the sciences, and) Tj T*
(indicates their social relation and relative perfection. In order to) Tj T*
(reach effective knowledge, the sciences must be studied in the order) Tj T*
(named; sociology cannot be understood without knowledge of the anterior) Tj T*
(sciences.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Behind and before all these sciences, however, lies the great science of) Tj T*
(mathematics--the most powerful instrument the mind can employ in the) Tj T*
(investigation of natural law--and the science of mathematics must be) Tj T*
(divided into abstract mathematics or the calculus, and concrete) Tj T*
(mathematics embracing general geometry and rational mechanics. We have) Tj T*
(thus really six great sciences.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(MATHEMATICS. Mathematics may be defined briefly as the indirect) Tj T*
(measurement of magnitudes and the determination of magnitudes by each) Tj T*
(other. It is the business of concrete mathematics to discover the) Tj T*
(_equations_ of phenomena; it is the business of abstract mathematics to) Tj T*
(educe results from the equations. Thus concrete mathematics discovers by) Tj T*
(actual experiment the acceleration which takes place per second in a) Tj T*
(falling body, and abstract mathematics educes results from the) Tj T*
(equations so discovered, and obtains unknown quantities from known.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(ASTRONOMY. Astronomy may be defined as the science by which we discover) Tj T*
(the laws of the geometrical and mechanical phenomena presented by) Tj T*
(heavenly bodies. To discover these laws we can use only our sense of) Tj T*
(sight and our reasoning power, and reasoning bears a greater proportion) Tj T*
(to observation here than in any other science. Sight alone would never) Tj T*
(teach us the figure of the earth or the path of a planet, and only by) Tj T*
(the measurement of angles and computation of times can we discover) Tj T*
(astronomical laws. The observation of these invariable laws frees man) Tj T*
(from servitude to the theological and metaphysical conceptions of the) Tj T*
(universe.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PHYSICS. Physics may be defined briefly as the study of the laws which) Tj T*
(regulate the general properties of bodies regarded _en masse_, their) Tj T*
(molecules remaining unaltered and usually in a state of aggregation. In) Tj T*
(the observations of physics all the senses are employed, and) Tj T*
(mathematical analysis and experiment assist observation. In the) Tj T*
(phenomena of astronomy human intervention was impossible; in the) Tj T*
(phenomena of physics man begins to modify natural phenomena.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Physics includes the subdivisions statics, dynamics, thermology,) Tj T*
(acoustics, optics, and electrology. Physics is still handicapped by) Tj T*
(metaphysical conceptions of the primary causes of phenomena.) Tj T*
