() Tj T*
(CHEMISTRY. Chemistry may be briefly defined as the study of the laws of) Tj T*
(the phenomena of composition and decomposition, which result from the) Tj T*
(molecular and specific mutual action of different substances, natural or) Tj T*
(artificial. In the observations of chemistry the senses are still more) Tj T*
(employed, and experiment is of still more utility. Even in chemistry) Tj T*
(metaphysical conceptions, such as "affinity," linger.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PHYSIOLOGY. Physiology may be defined as the study of the laws of) Tj T*
(organic dynamics in relation to structure and environment. Placed in a) Tj T*
(given environment, a definite organism must always act in a definite) Tj T*
(way, and physiology investigates the reciprocal relations between) Tj T*
(organism, environment, and function. In physiology observation and) Tj T*
(experiment are of the greatest value, and apparatus of all kinds is used) Tj T*
(to assist both observation and experiment. Physiology is most closely) Tj T*
(connected with chemistry, since all the phenomena of life are associated) Tj T*
(with compositions and decompositions of a chemical character.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_II.--Social Physics_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To place social physics on a scientific basis is a task of great) Tj T*
(difficulty, since social theories are still perverted by theological and) Tj T*
(metaphysical doctrines. All I can hope to do is to point out general) Tj T*
(principles which may serve to correct the intellectual anarchy which is) Tj T*
(the cause of the moral and political anarchy of the present day. I) Tj T*
(propose to state first how the institution of a science of social) Tj T*
(physics bears upon the principal needs and grievances of society, so) Tj T*
(that men worthy of the name of statesmen may realise that such labours) Tj T*
(are of real utility. So far, positive philosophy has worked timidly and) Tj T*
(tentatively, and has not been bold and broad and general enough to cope) Tj T*
(with intellectual anarchy in social questions; but it is necessary now) Tj T*
(that it play a more dominant part in life, and lead society out of the) Tj T*
(turmoil in which it has tossed for three centuries.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At present, society is distracted by two conflicting influences, which) Tj T*
(may be called the theological polity and the metaphysical polity.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The theological polity at one time exercised a beneficent influence on) Tj T*
(society; but for three centuries past its influence has been essentially) Tj T*
(retrograde, and has gradually, but radically, decayed. The causes of its) Tj T*
(decline are various; but the chief present-day antagonist to the) Tj T*
(theological polity is the scientific spirit, and the scientific spirit) Tj T*
(can now never be repressed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The metaphysical polity is progressive, but progressive mainly in a) Tj T*
(negative way. So far, it has made for progress; but it has made for) Tj T*
(progress chiefly by removing impediments to progress, by destroying the) Tj T*
(theological conceptions which retarded the development of human) Tj T*
(intelligence and human society. Though dangerous and revolutionary, it) Tj T*
(has been necessary; for much required to be demolished to permit) Tj T*
(permanent reconstruction.) Tj T*
ET
