() Tj T*
(Society, however, cannot be regarded as composed of individuals. The) Tj T*
(true social unit is the _family_; it is essentially on the plan of the) Tj T*
(family that society is constructed. In a family the social and the) Tj T*
(personal instincts are blended and reconciled; in a family, too, the) Tj T*
(principle of subordination and mutual co-operation is exemplified. The) Tj T*
(domestic is the basis of all social life. The modern tendency,) Tj T*
(therefore, to attack the institution of the family is an alarming) Tj T*
(symptom of social disorganisation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The sociological basis of the family depends on subordination of sexes) Tj T*
(and of ages.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Marriage at once satisfies, disciplines, and harmonises the strongest) Tj T*
(and most disorderly instinct of our animal nature; and though it may be) Tj T*
(attacked by the revolutionary spirit because of its theological) Tj T*
(implications, yet the institution is based on true principles, and must) Tj T*
(survive. No doubt marriage has been modified, but to modify is not to) Tj T*
(overthrow, and its fundamental principle remains intact.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The fundamental principle of the institution of marriage is the natural) Tj T*
(subordination of the woman--a principle which has reappeared under all) Tj T*
(forms of marriage. Biology teaches that radical differences, physical) Tj T*
(and moral, distinguish the sexes, and sociology will prove that the) Tj T*
(much-advertised equality of sexes is a fiction, and that equality of the) Tj T*
(sexes would be incompatible with all social existence. Each sex has) Tj T*
(special functions it must perform in the family, and the necessary) Tj T*
(subordination of one sex is in no wise injurious, since the happiness of) Tj T*
(every being depends on the wise development of its proper nature.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Our social system depends on intellectual activity under affective) Tj T*
(stimulus, and in power of mental labour the woman is incontestably) Tj T*
(inferior to the man, either because her mental powers are weaker, or) Tj T*
(because her lively moral and physical sensibility is unfavourable to) Tj T*
(mental concentration.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Besides the bond of marriage, which holds together society, there is the) Tj T*
(bond between parents and children. Here again we find the principle of) Tj T*
(subordination in force, and even as we find wild revolutionaries who) Tj T*
(challenge the principle of subordination in women, so there are some who) Tj T*
