(The spontaneous subordination in the human family is the best model for) Tj T*
(society. On the other hand, we see obedience and due subordination) Tj T*
(allied to gratitude, and unassociated with shame; and, on the other) Tj T*
(hand, we see absolute authority combined with affection and geniality.) Tj T*
(There are those who would take children from their parents' care, and) Tj T*
(hand them over to society, and there are those who would prevent the) Tj T*
(transmission of property from parents to children; but such) Tj T*
(extravagances need not be examined here.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Coming now to the consideration of society as constructed out of the) Tj T*
(family units, we see unity of aim associated with diversity of) Tj T*
(functions. It is a marvellous spectacle to see how in a society the) Tj T*
(individuals pursuing each their own end yet unconsciously co-operate;) Tj T*
(and this co-operation is the mainspring of society. In the family,) Tj T*
(co-operation is much less marked; for the family is founded chiefly on) Tj T*
(affection, and in affection finds its justification, quite apart from) Tj T*
(co-operation towards any end. In society the instinct of co-operation) Tj T*
(preponderates, and the instinct of affection plays only a secondary) Tj T*
(part. There are exceptional men in whom the affective side of the social) Tj T*
(instinct is dominant; but such men in most cases give their affection) Tj T*
(to the race at large simply from lack of domestic sympathy.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The principle of co-operation, spontaneous or concerted, is the basis of) Tj T*
(society, and the object of society must ever be to find the right place) Tj T*
(for its individual members in its great co-operative scheme. There is,) Tj T*
(however, a danger of exaggerated specialism; it concentrates the) Tj T*
(attention of individuals on small parts of the social machine, and thus) Tj T*
(narrows their sense of the social community, and produces an) Tj T*
(indifference to the larger interests of humanity. It is lamentable to) Tj T*
(find an artisan spending his life making pin-heads, and it is equally) Tj T*
(lamentable to find a man with mind employing his mind only in the) Tj T*
(solution of equations.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To guard against such social and intellectual disintegration must be the) Tj T*
(duty of government. It must foster the feeling of interconnection) Tj T*
(between individuals; and such a bond of feeling must be intellectual and) Tj T*
(moral rather than material, and will always imply subordination. The) Tj T*
(social instinct of man spontaneously produces government, and there is a) Tj T*
(much stronger instinct of obedience in man than is commonly supposed.) Tj T*
(Who has not felt it good to resign the responsibility of conduct to wise) Tj T*
(and trustworthy guidance? Even in revolutionary times the people feel) Tj T*
(the need of preponderant authority, and political subordination is as) Tj T*
(inevitable as it is indispensable.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_IV.--Social Dynamics_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Human progress consists essentially in the evolution of the moral and) Tj T*
(intellectual qualities proper to man. Most of the occupations of) Tj T*
(civilisation which deal with material things relieve man from material) Tj T*
(cares and discomforts, and permit him to use his higher faculties.) Tj T*
