(Death, too, may be considered a promoter of human progress. Youth is) Tj T*
(essentially progressive, age essentially conservative and opposed to) Tj T*
(progress, and death it is that prevents old age from too seriously) Tj T*
(impeding the progress of the world. If life were ten times as long,) Tj T*
(progress would be greatly retarded. On the other hand, death interferes) Tj T*
(with continuity of work, and by interrupting a man's work often delays) Tj T*
(its fruition. It is probable that if life were twice or thrice as long,) Tj T*
(progress would be more rapid.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Human progress is directed by the reason, and the history of the) Tj T*
(progress of society is largely the history of the human mind in its) Tj T*
(progress through its three stages--the theological, metaphysical, and) Tj T*
(positive. The necessity of these stages can be shown.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At first man knows nothing but himself, and it was inevitable that he) Tj T*
(should explain things as produced by a being like himself. The) Tj T*
(theological philosophy gave a basis for observation by its hypotheses) Tj T*
(that phenomena were products of actions like human acts, and that all) Tj T*
(bodies had life like human life, and that there was an invisible world) Tj T*
(with invisible agents. These hypotheses were not only intellectually) Tj T*
(necessary; they were also morally necessary, for they gave man) Tj T*
(confidence to act, and hope that he could modify anything unsatisfactory) Tj T*
(in the universe by appeals to its maker. Not only did the theological) Tj T*
(philosophy sustain man's courage, and kindle his hope, and increase his) Tj T*
(sense of power, but it gave an intellectual unanimity of great social) Tj T*
(and political value; and, producing a special speculative class, made) Tj T*
(the first effective division between things of matter and things of) Tj T*
(mind. Except for the theological speculative class, man might have) Tj T*
(remained merely a superior monkey.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Still, the theological philosophy was obviously only temporary, and) Tj T*
(could not satisfy the needs of more highly developed intelligence, and) Tj T*
(it soon came into conflict with positive philosophy. Indeed, at all) Tj T*
(times there had been glimmerings of positive belief, for at all times) Tj T*
(the simplest phenomena had been considered subject to natural laws, and) Tj T*
(all had been compelled to act in everyday affairs on the assumption of) Tj T*
(the invariability of natural law. The positive philosophy, therefore,) Tj T*
(was inevitable from the first, and its open antagonism to the) Tj T*
(theological philosophy was merely a question of time.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Between the theological and positive philosophy naturally and) Tj T*
(necessarily has intervened the metaphysical, which has substituted) Tj T*
(entities for a deity. This philosophy has never had the social power or) Tj T*
(the consistency of the theological philosophy; its entities have been) Tj T*
(mere abstractions. It has and has had such political power simply) Tj T*
(because so elusive.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Material progress has gone through similar stages. The primitive) Tj T*
(tendency of mankind was to a military life. At first the military life) Tj T*
(afforded man, apart from cannibalism, the easy means of making a living;) Tj T*
(and in no other school in these days could order have been taught, and) Tj T*
(in no other way could political consolidation be so quickly effected.) Tj T*
