(The law of interest is that the relation between wages and interest is) Tj T*
(determined by the average power of increase which attaches to capital) Tj T*
(from its use in its reproductive modes. The law of wages is that they) Tj T*
(depend upon the margin of production, or upon the produce which labour) Tj T*
(can obtain at the highest point of natural productiveness open to it) Tj T*
(without the payment of rent. This law of wages accords with and explains) Tj T*
(universal facts, and shows that where land is free, and labour is) Tj T*
(unassisted by capital, the whole produce will go to labour as wages.) Tj T*
(Where land is free, and labour is assisted by capital, wages will) Tj T*
(consist of the whole produce, less that part necessary to induce the) Tj T*
(storing up of labour as capital. Where land is subject to ownership and) Tj T*
(rent arises, wages will be fixed by what labour can secure from the) Tj T*
(highest natural opportunities open to it without the payment of rent.) Tj T*
