(_III.--The Common Right to Land_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The fact that the speculative advance in land values cuts down the) Tj T*
(earnings of labour and capital, and checks production, leads) Tj T*
(irresistibly to the conclusion that this is the main cause of those) Tj T*
(periodical industrial depressions to which every civilised country seems) Tj T*
(increasingly liable.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Robbed of all the benefits of the increase of productive power, labour) Tj T*
(is exposed to certain effects of advancing civilisation which, without) Tj T*
(the advantages that naturally accompany them, are positive evils, and of) Tj T*
(themselves tend to reduce the free labourer to the helpless and degraded) Tj T*
(condition of the slave. As land is necessary to the exertion of labour) Tj T*
(in the production of wealth, to command the land is to command all the) Tj T*
(fruits of labour save enough to enable labour to exist. But there is) Tj T*
(also an active, energetic power--a power that in every country, be its) Tj T*
(political form what it may, writes laws and moulds thought--the power of) Tj T*
(a vast and dominant pecuniary interest. The great cause in the) Tj T*
(inequality of the distribution of wealth is the inequality in the) Tj T*
(ownership of land. The ownership of land is the great fundamental fact) Tj T*
(which ultimately determines the social and political, and consequently,) Tj T*
(the intellectual and moral condition of a people. The tendencies and) Tj T*
(measures at present relied on or advocated as calculated to relieve) Tj T*
(poverty and distress among the masses are insufficient. The true remedy) Tj T*
(is to substitute for individual the common ownership of land.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As man belongs to himself, so his labour when put in concrete form) Tj T*
(belongs to him. As nature gives only to labour, the exertion of labour) Tj T*
(in production is the only title to exclusive possession. When) Tj T*
(non-producers can claim as rent a portion of the wealth created by) Tj T*
(producers, the right of the producers to the fruits of their labour is) Tj T*
(to that extent denied.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The equal right of all men to the use of land is as clear as their equal) Tj T*
(right to breathe the air--it is a right proclaimed by the fact of their) Tj T*
(existence. The right of individual proprietorship of land is the denial) Tj T*
(of the natural rights of other individuals--it is a wrong which must) Tj T*
(show itself in the inequitable division of wealth. Again, the ownership) Tj T*
(of land will always give the ownership of men, to a degree measured by) Tj T*
(the necessity, real or artificial, for the use of land. And when that) Tj T*
