(THOMAS HOBBES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Leviathan) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(     Thomas Hobbes was born at Malmesbury, Wiltshire, England, April 5,) Tj T*
(     1588, and died at Hardwick Dec. 4, 1679. When comparatively a young) Tj T*
(     man he was secretary to Francis Bacon. He spent many years abroad,) Tj T*
(     met Galileo, and corresponded with Descartes. But he did not begin) Tj T*
(     to produce until in advanced middle age. "Leviathan, or the Matter,) Tj T*
(     Form, and Power of a Commonwealth, Ecclesiastical and Civil,") Tj T*
(     appeared in 1651. His special impulse to the construction of a) Tj T*
(     science of politics came from the Great Rebellion, his detestation) Tj T*
(     of the principles on which it was based, and his dissatisfaction) Tj T*
(     with the theory of "divine right" as a bafis for the absolutism) Tj T*
(     which he counted a necessity. The "Leviathan" is the commonwealth,) Tj T*
(     or state, conceived as an "artificial man," and this gives the) Tj T*
(     title to this famous work. But this essay towards a science of) Tj T*
(     politics was only a fragment of that complete and all-inclusive) Tj T*
(     structure which he contemplated. Although in this sense only a) Tj T*
(     fragment, it has largely influenced all political theorising since) Tj T*
(     his day: and it contains the most definite enunciation of the) Tj T*
(     doctrine of the social contract, which took so different and so) Tj T*
(     revolutionary a shape in the hands of Rousseau.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_I.--Of Man_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
