(     active part in Florentine politics, and was employed on numerous) Tj T*
(     diplomatic missions. A keen student of the politics of his time, he) Tj T*
(     was also an ardent patriot. The exigencies of party warfare drove) Tj T*
(     him into temporary retirement, during which he produced a number of) Tj T*
(     brilliant plays and historical studies; but the most notable of his) Tj T*
(     achievements is "The Prince." "The Prince" may be regarded as the) Tj T*
(     first modern work treating of politics as a science. The one) Tj T*
(     question to which the author devotes himself is: How a prince may) Tj T*
(     establish and maintain the strongest possible government. Moral) Tj T*
(     principles, therefore, must yield entirely to the dictates of pure) Tj T*
