(published by the National Assembly as the basis of the French) Tj T*
(constitution. But does he mean to deny that _man_ has any rights? If he) Tj T*
(does, then he must mean that there are no such things as rights) Tj T*
(anywhere; for who is there in the world but man? But if Mr. Burke means) Tj T*
(to admit that man has rights, the question then will be: What are those) Tj T*
(rights and how came man by them originally?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The error of those who reason by precedents drawn from antiquity) Tj T*
(respecting the rights of man is that they do not go far enough into) Tj T*
(antiquity; they stop in some of the intermediate stages, and produce) Tj T*
(what was then done as a rule for the present day. Mr. Burke, for) Tj T*
