(monarchs for ever, because an English Parliament did make such a) Tj T*
(submission to William and Mary, not only on behalf of the people then) Tj T*
(living, but on behalf of their heirs and posterities--as if any) Tj T*
(parliament had the right of binding and controlling posterity, or of) Tj T*
(commanding for ever how the world should be governed. If antiquity is to) Tj T*
(be authority, a thousand such authorities may be produced, successively) Tj T*
(contradicting each other; but if we proceed on, we shall at last come) Tj T*
(out right; we shall come to the time when man came from the hand of his) Tj T*
(Maker. What was he then? Man! Man was his high and only title, and a) Tj T*
(higher cannot be given him.) Tj T*
