(government. It has its origin in the principles of society and the) Tj T*
(natural constitution of man. The mutual dependence and reciprocal) Tj T*
(interest which man has upon man, and all the parts of civilised) Tj T*
(community upon each other, create that great chain of connection which) Tj T*
(holds it together. In fine, society performs for itself almost) Tj T*
(everything which is ascribed to government, which is no farther) Tj T*
(necessary than to supply the few cases to which society and civilisation) Tj T*
(are not conveniently competent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
