(insufficient to meet the public expenditure they are supplemented by) Tj T*
(taxation. Every tax is finally paid from rent, profit or wages, or from) Tj T*
(all of them indifferently; and the chief principle to be observed in) Tj T*
(taxation is, that the subjects of the State ought to contribute towards) Tj T*
(the support of the government, as nearly as possible, in proportion to) Tj T*
